{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A route deviation is established on this trip's own trace. The governing measurement under POL-RD-01 is gps_trace.trace_distance_km, which is 26.44 km, against a booked optimal of 21.0 km — an excess of 5.44 km, which clears the 0.8 km absolute limb of the establishment test many times over.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02801", "EV-TRIP-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The percentage limb of POL-RD-01 also passes: the excess is 25.90% of the 21.0 km optimal route, above the 20% threshold. Both limbs must pass and both do. I have deliberately cited the trace figure (26.44 km, EV-GPS-02801) rather than the rounded 26.4 km convenience copy on the trip record, because POL-RD-01 says the trace governs where the two disagree.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02801", "EV-TRIP-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08(a) is discharged on the face of the bundle: trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip identifier TRP-02801, and the trip record's start timestamp (2026-08-13T08:33:21) matches the first GPS fix on the trace (2026-08-13T08:33:21). These artifacts describe the same trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02801", "EV-GPS-02801", "EV-FARE-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a) to (c): it runs 208 fixes at a 10 second sampling interval (well under the 30 second ceiling), reports zero gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds, and covers 100.0% of the trip. The independent-corroboration requirement of POL-RD-07(ii) is therefore not engaged, and neither is the mandatory escalation in POL-RD-10(3).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "point_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no rider-requested detour to excuse any part of the excess. The chat log for TRP-02801 contains 0 messages (message_count 0, first_message_at null, last_message_at null), and the trip record likewise records chat_message_count 0. With no rider instruction on file, the corroboration test in POL-RD-04 cannot be satisfied and the clause is unavailable; no distance is excluded before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02801", "EV-TRIP-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No pickup or dropoff relocation has occurred: pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null on the trip record, and amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min are both null. POL-RD-05 therefore cannot be run on this record and supplies no adjusted baseline.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This was not a pooled trip, so POL-RD-12 does not apply: trip_record.vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, and the matched-itinerary baseline that clause uses is not in play. The solo optimal of 21.0 km on the trip record is the correct baseline.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare was metered, not upfront-quoted, so POL-RD-11 does not close the distance-refund route: fare_breakdown.fare_model is METERED and fare_breakdown.quoted_fare_sgd is null. POL-RD-02 is the clause that governs the refund on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's only explanation — 'Traffic was heavy so I took another road', recorded in the counterparty statement — is an uncited traffic assertion. POL-RD-03 requires a traffic_advisory record naming a road the optimal route traverses with an overlapping validity window, and there is none: EV-ADVIS-02801-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so the comparison cannot be run and POL-RD-03 is unavailable. Under POL-RD-08 a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge the driver's burden. Under POL-RD-13 the missing advisory is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation either, because the driver names no evidence ID for an advisory and an assertion that cites no artifact cannot be invoked against one; the assertion is discarded and the deviation stands at the measured figure. I disclose that the artifact I rely on for the absence carries weight 0.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02801-01", "EV-TRIP-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-13"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own profile raises no corroboration hurdle: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1, well below the 4-claim trigger in POL-RD-08, so the additional-corroboration requirement that clause imposes on sub-30% claims does not apply here even if the excess were below 30%.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02801", "EV-GPS-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02 and comes out in the rider's favour. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 21.0 + 0.28 x 28.4) x 1.2 surge + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP + 0 waiting time fee - 0 promo = 33.8024. Refund = 40.71 charged_total - 33.8024 = 6.9076, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 = 6.95.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.refund_before_rounding",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The surge multiplier in that computation was read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, which is 1.2 — the only artifact on which the field appears — and not from any other source.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.surge_multiplier.value",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund of 6.9076 is far above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor, so NO_ACTION under that head is unavailable, and at 16.97% of charged_total it is below the 90% full-refund share, so the remedy POL-RD-02 licenses is a PARTIAL_REFUND of 6.95, not a full one.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.refund_share_of_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No pass-through correction arises under POL-RD-09 and none can be added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure: the fare breakdown carries zero ERP lines, zero tolls and no airport surcharge (the trip neither originates nor ends at an airport), so there is no off-route gantry and no phantom line to refund under POL-RD-09(4), and POL-RD-09(1) bars double-counting whatever the itemisation shows.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02801", "EV-GPS-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The deviation, though established, is not MATERIAL — 25.90% is below the 50% material_pct gate and 5.44 km is below the 8.0 km material_km gate — so I do not claim the POL-RD-06 uplift. For completeness, the driver's profile offers nothing that would aggravate the case in any event: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 191, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02801", "EV-GPS-02801", "EV-TRIP-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "NO_ACTION would be the wrong outcome here and would leave the rider carrying the whole charge: fare_breakdown.payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.0, so the present state is that the rider has paid 40.71 including the 6.91 attributable to the unjustified detour. Under POL-GEN-03 a PARTIAL_REFUND returning that portion is what the evidence supports.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02801"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

