    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 6.95,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the core arithmetic, and the record supports it. Under POL-RD-01 the governing distance is the GPS trace figure, gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 26.44 km (EV-GPS-02801), not the rounded 26.4 km convenience copy on the trip record, against the booked optimal of 21.0 km (EV-TRIP-02801). That is an excess of 5.44 km, or 25.9% — beyond both establishment gates of 0.8 km and 20% — so a route deviation is established. It is below both materiality gates of 8.0 km and 50%, so it is not a MATERIAL deviation and POL-RD-06 is not engaged: no FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) and no driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c). Consistently, the driver profile shows deviation_flags_90d = 0 over completed_trips_90d = 191, so no repeat pattern is established.\n\nThe refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02. That clause applies because the fare model is METERED (fare_breakdown.fare_model, EV-FARE-02801) and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-11 does not close the distance route. Surge is taken from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier = 1.2 — the only artifact carrying that field — and is not treated as absent. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 21.0 + 0.28 x 28.4) x 1.2 + 0.80 platform fee = (3.80 + 15.75 + 7.952) x 1.2 + 0.80 = 27.502 x 1.2 + 0.80 = 33.8024. Refund = charged_total 40.71 - 33.8024 = 6.9076, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 = 6.95. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and is 16.97% of charged_total, well below the 90% share that would convert this into a FULL_REFUND, so the outcome is a PARTIAL_REFUND of 6.95.\n\nNothing is added on top. The fare breakdown carries zero ERP lines, zero tolls, no airport surcharge and a 0.00 waiting-time fee, so POL-RD-09 yields no pass-through correction and no billing-integrity line; POL-RD-09(1) forbids adding off-route ERP to the POL-RD-02 figure in any event. No exculpatory clause reduces the excess: the chat log EV-CHAT-02801 holds 0 messages, so there is no POL-RD-04 rider instruction; the trip record shows pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at null and both amended optimals null, so POL-RD-05 cannot run; the vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply; and billed distance 26.4 km matches the traced 26.44 km, so no POL-RD-04 unbilled-distance compensation arises.\n\nThe driver's stated explanation in the counterparty statement — 'Traffic was heavy so I took another road' — is an uncited traffic assertion. Under POL-RD-13 it is tested against the traffic_advisory for this trip, and there is none on file: EV-ADVIS-02801-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. It neither reduces the excess nor supplies an amended optimal; the deviation stands at the measured figure under POL-RD-13(2). Because the driver named no evidence ID for an advisory, the absence is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so it is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation.\n\nThe GPS trace is not impaired for policy purposes: 208 fixes at a 10-second interval, zero gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s and 100% coverage, so POL-RD-07(a)-(c) and the escalation in POL-RD-10(3) are not engaged. Trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown (TRP-02801) and the timestamps are consistent, and the refund is under both SGD 150.00 and charged_total, so no POL-RD-10 trigger fires. The rider's profile (deviation_claims_60d = 1) adds no corroboration hurdle.\n\nThe confidence cap is 1.00: every artifact carrying the deciding facts — EV-GPS-02801, EV-TRIP-02801 and EV-FARE-02801 — has weight_multiplier 1.0, and the only impaired artifact, the missing advisory, carries nothing. The monetary effect of 6.95 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so this provisional ruling is executed automatically, subject to appeal under POL-GEN-04. No clause produces a referral on these facts."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

